  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Lowest ketone is $\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{COCH}_3$ (which form an oxime) and its next homologue is $\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{COCH}_3$ which form oxime with $\\mathrm{NH}_2 \\mathrm{OH}$. Such oxime shows the property of geometrical isomerism, i.e., it shows two isomers, symmetric and antisymmertic. (These are differ w.r.t. arrangement towards the space of $-\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{N}$, their different behaviour, can be confirmed with the help of Beckmann's rearrangement.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/EWRM37fa9BtKe7lTnyup6dAulowJ4gn46tYeyO_eSUE.original.fullsize.png\"><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/piTLmcB5fVTIitK6u_WWUOlNpuukGwUWmlkLBHrK3qA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
